Z||000000||pepper||10-11-2001||03:56 PM||||hi you guys<BR>I'm thinking about to buy a fiero.<BR>this are my demands<BR>-V6<BR>-second edition fiero 87 or 88<BR>-much aftermarket parts available<BR>-and if its possible T-roof<P>i have to know some things<BR>what's the difference between GT en SE,<BR>what's the difference between 87 and 88<BR>what would be the best choice and why<P>I saw a picture named 49048088_012178_339x203.jpg<BR>the whit one with the diablo nose<BR>in the case mods<BR>what kind of fiero is that?<BR>can someone give me a website for more pix of that car? <P>please help me !<P>bryce<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Steve Normington||10-11-2001||04:07 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by pepper:<BR><B>-V6<BR>-second edition fiero 87 or 88<BR>-much aftermarket parts available<BR>-and if its possible T-roof<P>i have to know some things<BR>what's the difference between GT en SE,<BR>what's the difference between 87 and 88<BR>what would be the best choice and why<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>There are a limited number of V-6's available.<BR>There is no "second edition" that I know of. <BR>An 84-87 would probably have more after parts available.<BR>T-Tops exist for both years.<BR><A HREF="http://www.fiero.org/spotter.html" TARGET=_blank>This website</A> has a spotters guide for the difference between an SE and a GT. Most GT's are fastbacks (the sloping rear) All SE's are notchbacks (the steeper rear).<BR>An 88 has better suspension than an 87. An 87 will probably have more parts available.<BR>An 88 GT T-Top V-6 is probably one of the rarer versions and will probably be more expensive.||||reg||1
Z||000002||GTFiero1||10-11-2001||04:33 PM||||you can buy the diablo nose at <A HREF="http://www.cybercars.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cybercars.com</A>   and go into the Pisa section, its called the Arteero nose. its on a fastback GT. there is no difference between an 86-87 GT. the 88 GT's engine was modified very little (changed to externally balanced) the 88's will be the best handleing ones but the most expensive. T-tops came from the factory only in 88 but other companies have put T-tops on other years. from what i understand the t-top seals are getting rare. there are plenty of aftermarket parts available- <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A>   has performance parts for the 2.8 6-cyl<P>------------------<BR>Adam J. B.||||reg||1
